eMutability":"nonpayable","type":"function"},{"inputs":[{"internalType":"address","name":"_owner","type":"address"}],"name":"setOwner","outputs":[],"stateMutability":"nonpayable","type":"function"},{"inputs":[{"internalType":"uint256","name":"id","type":"uint256"},{"internalType":"uint256","name":"perSecond","type":"uint256"}],"name":"setRate","outputs":[],"stateMutability":"nonpayable","type":"function"},{"inputs":[{"internalType":"address","name":"_releaser","type":"address"}],"name":"setReleaser","outputs":[],"stateMutability":"nonpayable","type":"function"},{"inputs":[{"internalType":"uint256","name":"id","type":"uint256"}],"name":"settleRefund","outputs":[],"stateMutability":"nonpayable","type":"function"}],"devdoc":{"details":"Each campaign has one funder, the manager who created it and deposited its whole budget. The engine never emits more than the budget, so the distributor can always be paid in full, and what was not emitted goes back to the funder once the campaign ended. More rewards for a pool are a new campaign on the same pool, so a budget never mixes the tokens of two wallets. The bot refuses campaign changes that would alter what an already published week emitted, and every change here takes effect from the block that makes it, so none can: - A campaign is never removed, and its pool, reward token, `minWidthTicks` and funder never change. Its budget   only drops, when a refund sends what the campaign cannot emit back to the funder. - A campaign starts when it is created, and a rate change applies from the block it is mined in. Rate history   is append-only; a rate of 0 ends the campaign for good, so its rates bound everything it can still emit. Reward tokens must transfer exactly the amount requested: fee-on-transfer and rebasing tokens are not supported. The registry records the nominal budget and every campaign of a token shares one balance, so such a token would pay one campaign's releases and refund out of the escrow of the others. Reward tokens must also never revert a transfer, so tokens with a pause, a blocklist or transfer hooks are not supported either. `release` pays every due campaign in one call, so one failing transfer would stop the release and the weekly root of every campaign on the chain, and a blocked funder would never get its refund. Managers are trusted team wallets. `createCampaign` checks neither the token nor that the pool uses the Seer hook, and the bot replays each pool from the hook deployment, so an older pool would stop it for every campaign.","errors":{"SafeERC20FailedOperation(address)":[{"details":"An operation with an ERC-20 token failed."}]},"events":{"CampaignSet(uint256,(bytes32,address,uint256,uint32,(uint64,uint256)[]))":{"details":"Emitted with the whole campaign after every change, so the state at any block can be rebuilt from logs."}},"kind":"dev","methods":{"constructor":{"params":{"_distributor":"This chain's Universal Rewards Distributor.","_managers":"The initial managers.","_owner":"The owner of the registry, usually a Safe.","_releaser":"The rewards bot, or the zero address to set it later."}},"createCampaign(bytes32,address,uint256,uint256,uint32)":{"returns":{"id":"The id of the new campaign."}},"release(uint256[],uint256[],uint64)":{"details":"A total below what was already released sends nothing: the release stays, as the distributor cannot return it."},"settleRefund(uint256)":{"details":"Until the bot releases a week whose cutoff is at or after the end, the emission since the last release is unknown here, so the budget keeps the most the rates can have emitted since then and the rest goes back at once. Once that week is released, a second call sends back what the campaign did not emit after all. The engine never emits more than the rates do, so the final release always fits in the budget that is kept."}},"stateVariables":{"MAX_WIDTH_TICKS":{"details":"`TickMath.MAX_TICK - TickMath.MIN_TICK` of Uniswap V4: no position is wider, so a larger minimum width would leave every position out and the campaign would never emit."},"funders":{"details":"By campaign id: the wallet that deposited the budget, which changes the campaign and gets its refund. Kept apart from `Campaign` so `CampaignSet` carries only what the bot reads."}},"title":"RewardCampaigns","version":1},"userdoc":{"kind":"user","methods":{"createCampaign(bytes32,address,uint256,uint256,uint32)":{"notice":"Creates a campaign that emits `perSecond` from this block on, and deposits its whole `budget` from the caller, who must have approved this contract for it and becomes its funder."},"getCampaigns()":{"notice":"Every campaign, in id order."},"getFunders()":{"notice":"The funder of every campaign, in id order."},"getReleases()":{"notice":"The release state of every campaign, in id order."},"release(uint256[],uint256[],uint64)":{"notice":"Sends the distributor what campaigns `ids` emitted up to the weekly cutoff `upTo`, given as the cumulative `emitted` of each, so a repeated call sends nothing more."},"setOwner(address)":{"notice":"Transfers ownership. It takes effect at once."},"setRate(uint256,uint256)":{"notice":"Sets the rate from this block on. A rate of 0 ends the campaign for good: more rewards for the pool are a new campaign."},"settleRefund(uint256)":{"notice":"Sends what an ended campaign cannot have emitted back to its funder. Anyone may call it, since the tokens can only go to the funder, so a funder who is no longer a manager still gets them."}},"notice":"Liquidity reward campaigns of Seer's Uniswap V4 pools on this chain, and the escrow of their budgets. Rewards pay out on the pool's chain, so there is one registry per chain with pools, next to that chain's Morpho Universal Rewards Distributor. The weekly rewards bot (`packages/seer-pm-rewards`) rebuilds the campaigns from `CampaignSet` events up to each Monday cutoff, releases what each one emitted to the distributor and then submits the root that lets users claim it.","version":1}},"settings":{"compila